# What never goes into the image.
#
# `.env` first and loudest. It holds the local database URL, config.py reads it
# at import time, and a copy of it inside the image would quietly outrank
# nothing — but it would ship a credential to a registry, and production's
# DATABASE_URL is meant to arrive from the environment instead. The Dockerfile
# copies only `app`, so this is the second lock rather than the first; it is
# here so that the day someone writes `COPY . .` it still holds.
.env
.env.*

# Tests, tooling and caches: none of it runs in production, and the bytecode is
# compiled for whichever machine built the thing rather than for this one.
#
# The `**/` matters. A bare `__pycache__/` matches a directory at the top of the
# context and nowhere else, so `app/__pycache__` shipped until this said so.
tests/
pyproject.toml
requirements-dev.txt
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
